                                "sense_id": "c33da8cc-1a14-3370-b505-4481eb4711fe",
                                "text": "The infant, while it lieth in the darke priſon of the mothers wombe, never quatcheth nor weepeth ; but as ſoone as ever it commeth out of the womb into the light, it knits the browes, and wrings the eyes, and cries"
